  "schema": "primestruct_benchmark_baseline_v1",
  "notes": "Baseline thresholds for benchmark regression checks. primestruct_vm runs primevm at its default -O2 (the threaded fast kernel plus the optimizer; the time includes compiling the source) and primestruct_native runs -O2 native code (register allocation on x86_64). Their limits sit about three to four times above the measured means (2026-10-04, Linux x86_64: native 4.0/6.8/16.9 ms and vm 62/78/153 ms for aggregate/json_scan/json_parse), so losing register allocation, the fast kernel or an optimizer pass fails them while ordinary machine noise does not. call_fib (recursive calls) and float_series (f64 arithmetic) were added 2026-10-04 with native 16/63 ms and vm 141/650 ms. primestruct_optexe and primestruct_native are optional rows.",
